  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output 7.5. Increased capacity of constituents to develop fair and effective labour migration frameworks, institutions and services to protect migrant workers</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Seafarers in Tuvalu have increased practical skills and theoretical knowledge relating to seafaring, and are better positioned to access decent work opportunities and safe labour migration opportunities. Through a partnership with the Tuvalu Maritime Training Institute, 57 Seafarers, approximately 7% of the seafarers in Tuvalu, have completed a comprehensive training course focused on improving skills and safety awareness at sea.  

The training was delivered through the existing  and longstanding Maritime Training Institute of Tuvalu, thus contributing to the sustainability of this initiative. 

The Department of Labour, Ministry of Public Works, Infrastructure, Environment, Labour, Meteorology and Disaster in the Government of Tuvalu has highlighted that supporting the refresher training &#x2018;has not only empowered the pool of seafarers but has also given them hope for job security, sustainability in terms of tackling the effects of Covid-19 on their families, communities and the nation as a whole.&apos; Seafarers refresher training: Through the &#x2018;Pacific Climate Change Migration and Human Security Programme&apos; and the &#x2018;Enhancing food security and building socio-economic resilience to Covid-19 in Tuvalu&#x2018;  Projects, and in partnership with IOM,  ILO supported two cohorts of 25 and 32 seafarers to undertake a Seafarer refresher training course. The 4-week intensive course focuses on maritime safety and directly contributes to the protection of seafarers at sea. The course was delivered by the Tuvalu Maritime Training Institute.</narrative>
   </description>
